  "layout_note": "Two-column BACKMATTER of the 1582 Rheims NT: running PROSE (role 'prose', NOT a gridded/cell table), so no ' | ' column separators. It is a polemical 'Table' of the Protestant translators' corruptions, arranged by chapter & verse: Actes of the Apostles ch.2/3/9/14/15/16/17/19/20, then S. Paules Epiſtle to the Romanes ch.2/3/5. Centered running-title 'A TABLE OF' in spaced small caps. Two faces alternate within lines: ROMAN = the DR editors' own commentary; ITALIC = the quoted adversary translations / cited words (face is not separately encoded in the text field). PER-FACE w (project rule, verified by word-level zoom): ROMAN body uses a genuine single 'w' sort -> transcribed 'w' (words, new, alwaies, workes, were, we, which[roman], Wittenberge, away, where, wel, with, free-wil); ITALIC apparatus uses a double-v sort that renders as two separate v-strokes -> transcribed 'vv' (vvilt, vvhom, vvho, vvith, vvhen, vvhich, vvorſhip, vve, vvithout, vvorkes, lavv, vveake, tovvards). long-ſ is glyph-driven (worſhip, ſhrines, Engliſh read long-ſ). An italic section-header 'S. Paules Epiſtle to the Romanes:' introduces the Romans block, which opens with a 2-line woodcut decorated initial 'C' (drop_cap) giving 'CHAP. 2.'. Foot-of-page right-justified catchword 'comming,' (excluded from body concat). French spacing (a space before : ; and before some commas) preserved where the compositor set it; a few colons are set tight (deuotions:, Image:, God:, text:, men:and) and are transcribed without a preceding space. Digitization additions are NOT part of the page and are excluded: a red papal-keys shield + 'www.fatimamovement.com' watermark at lower-left, and scattered foxing/ink specks (several raised dots at line-ends are foxing, not points).",
